<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zahara de la Sierra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zahara de la Sierra is a village in the province of Cádiz, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, crowned by a Moorish castle above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadalete">Guadalete</a> valley. A frontier fortress between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and the Nasrid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, it was taken by Castile in 1407 and recaptured by the emir Abu al-Hasan Ali in December 1481, which Castile answered by seizing Alhama, starting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada-war">Granada War</a>. Castile retook it in 1483.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zahara-de-la-sierra.jpg" alt="Zahara de la Sierra" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lesamourai at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alcazaba_and_Town_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1481 the emir Abu al-Hasan Ali, known to Christians as Muley Hacén, seized the Castilian town of <b>Zahara</b>, and the Castilians replied by taking Alhama in 1482, opening the final Granada War.</blockquote><a href="/empire/emirate-of-granada">Emirate of Granada · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
